Falsifies `generational_table::verification::a_name_the_table_never_minted_resolves_to_nothing`.

The defect: the generation compare is reduced to the bounds check it is written on top of. `get`
on the slot already answers "is this a slot at all", so the `!=` looks like a second test of the
same thing to anyone who has not held the generation scheme in mind, and every name the table
itself minted still resolves correctly.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(Some(probe), minted)`, on any u64 whose low half is
a live slot index and whose high half is anything at all. A name may come from an untrusted
caller, so this is the forging case: the table would resolve a number nobody was ever issued.
diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 684df60..05f994a 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -253,9 +253,7 @@ impl<T, const N: usize> Table<T, N> {
         // A slot the target's `usize` cannot hold is no slot of any table there, so it resolves to
         // nothing rather than truncating onto a low slot that some live entry may hold.
         let slot = usize::try_from(slot).ok()?;
-        if *self.generations.get(slot)? != generation {
-            return None;
-        }
+        self.generations.get(slot)?;
         self.slots[slot].as_ref()?;
         Some(slot)
     }
